Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.70,0:00:16.75,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,I bring a report.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.75,0:00:20.67,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Details about the man who \Nrecently entered your service,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.67,0:00:23.09,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Don Orts, have come to light.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.58,0:00:26.27,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,He seems to be quite cleverly hiding it,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.27,0:00:30.68,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,but he—along with his parents—are \Nemployees of the First Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.96,0:00:32.73,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He's well-established there, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.28,0:00:38.78,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,The households of nobles, \Nespecially royalty,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.78,0:00:41.98,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,are managed quite strictly \Non various fronts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.82,0:00:45.22,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,In the interest of preserving \Nconfidentiality,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.22,0:00:48.63,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,there are often strict limits \Non who employees can interact with.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.50,0:00:55.28,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,In many cases, they marry other employees\Nper their master's recommendation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.28,0:00:59.01,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And children born to such marriages
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.01,0:01:01.56,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,also swear their loyalty to the master.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.71,0:01:09.04,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,I believe that the First Prince \Nsent him here as a spy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.04,0:01:10.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Probably.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.67,0:01:12.81,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Don't tell anyone what you've discovered.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.81,0:01:15.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Now that we know he's a spy,\Nwe can use him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.75,0:01:16.76,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.76,0:01:21.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The insight to recognize him as \Na spy during a first impression...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.23,0:01:22.89,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Your Highness never ceases to amaze me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.19,0:01:25.26,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm not sure I'd call it insight.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.26,0:01:28.32,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Even after I agreed to \Nlet him work for me,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:25.27,0:01:33.23,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,0)\an7\fs14\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFCF4&\3c&HCDAFA0&\bord0.75\blur1\b1\shad1\4c&H7D605F&\pos(14,20)}Name: Minister-Prince of Justice Noah Ararat \NSex: Male \NLevel: 3 / ∞ \N\NHP: E+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFire: F+B \NMP: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWater: E+S \NStrength: E+E\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWind: F \NStamina: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hEarth: F \NIntelligence: F+E\h\h\hLight: F \NSpirit: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDark: F \NSpeed: F+F \NDexterity: F+F
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.27,0:01:33.23,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,0)\an7\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&H7B6049&\3c&HF8D6AE&\4c&HB7775D&}m 0 0 l 258 0 258 75 0 75
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.32,0:01:30.88,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,my stats didn't increase.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.32,0:01:32.45,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That made it obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.22,0:01:37.41,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,Also, someone from the Bardsley store \Nhas requested an audience with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.41,0:01:40.75,Default,Dylan,0,0,0,,They say they have found the \Ntreasure you were seeking.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.75,0:01:41.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.97,0:01:45.26,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I guess that 10,000-rean \Nbait I gave him paid off.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.54,0:01:53.63,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Ah, if it isn't the Wise Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.63,0:01:56.17,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I pray this day finds you well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.46,0:01:57.88,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A good preface.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.18,0:01:59.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What have you found?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.98,0:02:01.77,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Ah, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.60,0:02:09.56,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I do hope it pleases Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.56,0:02:10.76,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A painting?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.76,0:02:12.87,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,That is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.42,0:02:32.29,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,A painting known as {\i1}Huwawa{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.29,0:02:34.69,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,It is the work of a renowned artist,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.69,0:02:37.63,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,but it is, of course, \Nno ordinary painting.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.42,0:02:44.22,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Is it cursed?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.82,0:02:48.13,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Most impressive, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.40,0:02:49.52,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Behold.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.09,0:03:04.96,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,This is a replica made around the \Nsame time {\i1}Huwawa{\i0} was painted.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.96,0:03:06.28,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A replica?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.50,0:03:08.62,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I can see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.62,0:03:11.50,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It looks like the same \Ngirl in both, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.58,0:03:15.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A cursed painting that matures?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.08,0:03:17.29,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Precisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.91,0:03:26.55,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Through Leviathan, I can \Ntell that the original
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.03,0:03:29.56,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,is giving off a strange aura.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.44,0:03:34.51,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In which case...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.44,0:03:36.87,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Y-Your Highness?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.17,0:04:06.85,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.27,0:04:28.57,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this?!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:43.59,0:04:45.55,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\c&H4F7C81&\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\pos(320,142.5)}Born Blessed, So I'll Obtain Ultimate Power
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.59,0:04:45.55,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\p1\bord2\c&H291505&\alpha&H255&\3c&H2986A5&\fscx87\pos(311,141.167)}m 0 0 l 235 0 l 225 8 l 235 15 l 18 15 l 30 8 l 18 0
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.83,0:06:08.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Uh-huh. Uh-huh. I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.26,0:06:11.84,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Huh? Y-You can understand \Nwhat she's saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.84,0:06:15.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes. She says this piece was \Npainted with her blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.58,0:06:20.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Its painter killed her while \Nshe was still a child
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.26,0:06:22.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and mixed her blood into the paint.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.03,0:06:24.74,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I had no idea...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.53,0:06:30.78,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,"I want to repay you for freeing me," eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.73,0:06:32.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.41,0:06:35.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,swear loyalty to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.09,0:06:39.05,Default,Huwawa,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.92,0:06:44.93,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I-Incredible...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.93,0:06:47.93,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I never thought a cursed painting \Ncould turn into this...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.28,0:06:57.02,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,So cutting her bonds with Leviathan
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.02,0:07:00.68,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,made it possible for her to enter \Nand leave her vessel at will?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.96,0:07:04.55,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,My earth magic gained a slight plus.
Dialogue: 1,0:07:01.98,0:07:09.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,0)\an7\fs14\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFCF4&\3c&HCDAFA0&\bord0.75\blur1\b1\shad1\4c&H7D605F&\pos(14,20)}Name: Minister-Prince of Justice Noah Ararat \NSex: Male \NLevel: 3 / ∞ \N\NHP: E+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFire: F+B \NMP: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWater: E+S \NStrength: E+E\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWind: F \NStamina: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hEarth: F+F \NIntelligence: F+E\h\h\hLight: F \NSpirit: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDark: F \NSpeed: F+F
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.98,0:07:09.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,0)\an7\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&H5E4E3C&\3c&HF8D6AE&\4c&HB7775D&}m 0 0 l 258 0 258 69 0 69
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.55,0:07:07.55,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That means she'll probably \Nbe useful in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.07,0:07:14.95,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,721)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 205)}Episode 9
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.07,0:07:14.95,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,721)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 225)}The Highest Trust
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.76,0:07:20.70,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well, give it a try, Huwawa.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.79,0:07:28.84,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.84,0:07:34.96,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I-Is... that... m-me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.96,0:07:37.01,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,She says she can do more, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.01,0:07:38.14,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.96,0:07:43.10,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Try touching her.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.54,0:07:50.72,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.72,0:07:53.90,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,My left hand can touch her, but \Nthe right hand passes through!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.69,0:07:58.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,She can make it work for both, \Nbut this is only a test.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.47,0:08:02.74,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I-Incredible... For someone I only \Nmet today to replicate me so well...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.26,0:08:07.38,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Well, the physical form is thanks \Nto her link with my armor ring,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.38,0:08:10.91,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,but I think this can definitely \Nbe called transformation magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.71,0:08:14.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well done. As thanks, I'll \Npay any price you name.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.44,0:08:17.54,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Contact me if you find anything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.54,0:08:18.65,Default,Bardsley,0,0,0,,I will!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.98,0:08:32.44,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&}Byron Alan \N{\fs13}Merchant
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.45,0:08:36.74,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What brings you here today? \NAnd what is that behind you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.01,0:08:39.82,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Ada has been honored with \NHis Majesty's favor
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.82,0:08:42.33,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,and officially accepted \Nas one of his attendants.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.00,0:08:46.72,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,This is merely a humble \Ntoken of my gratitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.72,0:08:48.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.79,0:08:52.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Ada is the girl Byron sent \Nto the palace as a servant.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.51,0:08:57.59,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,So the servant he chose six \Nyears ago, per my advice,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.59,0:08:59.61,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,has risen to the level of attendant.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.47,0:09:05.43,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I see. You really splurged, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.92,0:09:08.11,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's worth about 30,000 rean.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.32,0:09:10.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.56,0:09:13.86,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Oh, nothing... I'm just surprised \Nyou guessed the amount.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.86,0:09:15.27,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Brilliant as always!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.27,0:09:19.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,At any rate, that's good news. \NSo she starts as an attendant?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.04,0:09:22.99,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Yes. I'm hoping she'll achieve \Nthe status of wife eventually.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.27,0:09:24.15,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.87,0:09:27.78,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Consorts are divided into four ranks.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.83,0:09:41.51,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0.5\fs10\fade(487,0)\c&HFDFDFC&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(316,270)\3c&H000002&}Attendant
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.11,0:09:30.17,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,First are attendants, then concubines,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.50,0:09:41.51,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0.5\fs10\fade(487,0)\c&HFDFDFC&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\3c&H000002&\pos(316,200)}Concubine
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.17,0:09:32.02,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and above them are wives.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.42,0:09:41.51,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0.5\fs10\fade(487,0)\c&HFDFDFC&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\3c&H000002&\pos(316,130)}Wife
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.02,0:09:36.55,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And standing above all of them as the \Nemperor's legal wife is the empress.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.80,0:09:41.51,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord0.5\fs10\fade(487,0)\c&HFDFDFC&\fnTimes New Roman\b1\3c&H000002&\pos(316,58)}Empress
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.55,0:09:39.32,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,They rise in the ranks based on \Nhow much the emperor favors them
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.32,0:09:41.52,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and how high their sons rank.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.34,0:09:45.84,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Noah's mother reached the rank of wife
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.84,0:09:49.19,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,when the emperor granted \NNoah his "Wise" title.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.18,0:09:46.98,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an1\fade(0,322)\fs32\shad5\fnTimes New Roman\b1\bord0.5\blur1.5\c&HFAF7F5&\3c&HD6C5A8&\4c&HAC896D&\frx30\fry358\pos(50.667,146.667)}Thirteenth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.50,0:09:47.60,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(503,0)\an1\fs32\shad5\fnTimes New Roman\b1\bord0.5\blur1.5\c&HFAF7F5&\3c&HD6C5A8&\4c&HAC896D&\frx30\fry358\pos(50.667,146.667)}Wise Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.19,0:09:52.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It goes without saying that \Nthere's only one empress.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.23,0:09:55.70,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So if you're aiming for the top, the \Nrank of wife is as high as she can go.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.70,0:09:56.67,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.23,0:10:01.33,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,All I can do now is pray that she earns \Nmore and more of the emperor's favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.33,0:10:04.46,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No, it's all politics from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.75,0:10:09.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Of course, earning the emperor's favor \Nis the fastest way to get there,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.93,0:10:13.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but outside of that, what's important \Nis the politics among the consorts.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.96,0:10:15.73,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.73,0:10:16.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,For example...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.32,0:10:22.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,what if someone were to switch Ada's \Nperfume with a scent the emperor dislikes?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.97,0:10:26.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Based solely on how \Ncutthroat consorts can be,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.95,0:10:30.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,the inner palace is even more of a den \Nof demons than the world men live in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.98,0:10:33.21,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,I... I see!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.21,0:10:34.68,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Send her money.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.10,0:10:38.39,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Now that you know it's all politics, \Nyou know what you must do, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.76,0:10:41.66,Default,Byron,0,0,0,,Yes, of course! Thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.80,0:10:46.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Zoey.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.75,0:10:49.68,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Yes, Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.13,0:10:55.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Take this letter to my mother \Nalong with 10,000 rean.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.20,0:11:00.11,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,U-Um... wouldn't Dylan be a more \Nsuitable messenger to the palace?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.11,0:11:03.27,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Men are forbidden to enter the \Ninner palace where my mother is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.80,0:11:08.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's why I only see \Nher around once a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.03,0:11:11.15,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Princes are taken from their \Nmothers soon after they're born.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.15,0:11:13.79,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Only once... a year?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.64,0:11:16.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And please give my mother \Na message for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.97,0:11:19.79,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Of course. What shall I tell her?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.19,0:11:23.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,"I consider myself Ada's guardian."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.17,0:11:27.28,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Y-You mean to use your\Nmother for politics?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.28,0:11:28.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.79,0:11:31.12,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,But... she's your mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.12,0:11:33.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,That's how the imperial family works.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.66,0:11:37.01,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Even between parent and child, profit \Nand status take priority over emotion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.45,0:11:39.53,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If Ada rises in the ranks,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.53,0:11:42.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,she could be a good ally to my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.82,0:11:45.92,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,What a... fascinating \Nworld you live in...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.24,0:11:50.77,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Understood. I will go at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.60,0:11:53.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,By the way...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.77,0:11:55.01,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.43,0:11:58.09,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,How is your mother doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.09,0:12:01.62,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,She is forever grateful that you \Ngave her a home in the capital
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.62,0:12:05.48,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,and even gave her a job.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.25,0:12:07.51,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.13,0:12:14.50,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Oh, nothing. She said she might have \Nimagined it, so it isn't worth mentioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.90,0:12:16.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It isn't nothing. Tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.30,0:12:17.87,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,A-All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.60,0:12:23.80,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Part of my mother's job is to open and \Nclose the gate every morning and night.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.80,0:12:28.30,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Yesterday, she heard a sound at night, \Nso she went to investigate...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.52,0:12:32.23,flashback,Martha,0,0,0,,I-Is someone there?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.02,0:12:37.73,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,She was unable to see them clearly,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.73,0:12:42.49,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,but she suspects there may be someone \Nsneaking in and out at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.49,0:12:45.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I see. You were right to inform me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.96,0:12:50.37,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,For now, tell your mother to say \Nnothing of this to anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.37,0:12:53.57,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Wha? Th-Then you think she imagined it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.02,0:12:55.84,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,We'll soon find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.69,0:13:22.84,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Today just wasn't your day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.10,0:13:29.91,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You're lucky to be alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.58,0:13:35.87,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Y-You mean someone... was \Ntrying to kill my mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.87,0:13:36.95,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.45,0:13:42.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,He must have thought she saw him leaving \Nthe mansion and tried to silence her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.00,0:13:44.75,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Well done, Huwawa.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.06,0:13:55.01,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Amazing... She was just \Nmy mother a moment ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.97,0:14:00.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Zoey.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.97,0:14:02.44,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Y-Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.44,0:14:06.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Return to Dosso with your mother's \N"body" for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.14,0:14:09.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Her hometown would be \Nthe place to bury her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.04,0:14:11.50,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.68,0:14:15.38,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It'll only {\i1}look{\i0} that way, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.17,0:14:18.16,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If she stays here,\Nshe'll be targeted again.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.68,0:14:22.83,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll send for you when this is all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.26,0:14:25.96,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Take some time off until \Nthen, just the two of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.41,0:14:29.68,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Master...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.68,0:14:33.14,Default,Martha,0,0,0,,Thank you so much! Thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.14,0:14:39.48,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,U-Um, but, Master... should we \Nreally let that man get away?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.48,0:14:43.02,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes. I have Huwawa monitoring him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.02,0:14:43.87,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.35,0:14:47.05,Default,Zoey,0,0,0,,You truly are amazing, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.54,0:14:59.84,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Where am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.84,0:15:01.38,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So you're awake.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.67,0:15:05.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Take it easy. You nearly died.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.99,0:15:07.40,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I... did?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.40,0:15:09.14,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You don't remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.87,0:15:13.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,After reporting that you'd \Nkilled the woman who saw you,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.24,0:15:18.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,you were stabbed by a go-between.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.18,0:15:23.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In other words, you failed \Nin your role as a spy,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.49,0:15:25.39,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,so you were cast out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.02,0:15:30.24,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I had been monitoring you \Nbecause I expected this,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.24,0:15:32.57,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but I'm surprised you really did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.40,0:15:35.95,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.55,0:15:38.79,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And people are supposed \Nto be treasures...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.66,0:15:43.25,Default,Don,0,0,0,,You foresaw everything,\Nright down to my being cast out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.25,0:15:45.77,Default,Don,0,0,0,,You are indeed the\NWise Prince they say you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.77,0:15:47.70,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I am in awe of your keen insight.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.50,0:15:56.21,Default,Don,0,0,0,,If I had been employed by you from \Nthe start, and not as a spy...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.21,0:15:58.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It's not too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.77,0:16:02.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You're saying that if things \Nhad worked out differently,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.04,0:16:04.72,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,you would be working for me now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.22,0:16:07.15,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If so, it's not too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.92,0:16:09.82,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.82,0:16:14.34,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But in return, I will punish betrayal \Neven more harshly than they did.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.34,0:16:18.64,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Once you've sworn loyalty to me,\Nyour life is mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.66,0:16:20.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.28,0:16:23.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I also won't cast you out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.98,0:16:34.60,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.00,0:16:37.40,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Please allow me to work for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.64,0:16:42.23,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,My wind stat gained a +F.
Dialogue: 1,0:16:39.64,0:16:44.73,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,100)\an7\fs14\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFCF4&\3c&HCDAFA0&\bord0.75\blur1\b1\shad1\4c&H7D605F&\pos(14,20)}Name: Minister-Prince of Justice Noah Ararat \NSex: Male \NLevel: 3 / ∞ \N\NHP: E+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFire: F+B \NMP: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWater: E+S \NStrength: E+E\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWind: F+F \NStamina: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hEarth: F+F \NIntelligence: F+E\h\h\h\hLight: F \NSpirit: F+F\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hDark: F \NSpeed: F+F \NDexterity: F+F \N Luck: F+F
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.64,0:16:44.73,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,0)\an7\bord2\shad2\blur1\p1\fscy220\alpha&H50&\c&H756C55&\3c&HF8D6AE&\4c&HB7775D&}m 0 0 l 258 0 258 81 0 81
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.23,0:16:44.91,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That proves he's genuinely \Nsworn his loyalty to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.73,0:16:47.06,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fade(399,0)\shad0\blur2\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFEFEFF&\3c&HB9977D&\frz6.96\t(0,2330,\fs25)\frx0\fry356\move(200,111,186,104,0,2317)}Water
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.73,0:16:47.06,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fade(399,0)\shad0\blur2\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HF8F8FC&\3c&HB9977D&\frz6.96\t(0,2330,\fs25)\frx0\fry356\move(213,209,202,209,0,2317)}Wind
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.73,0:16:47.06,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fade(399,0)\shad0\blur2\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFEFEFF&\3c&HB9977D&\frz6.96\t(0,2330,\fs25)\frx0\fry356\move(230,305,220,316,0,2317)}Earth
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.34,0:16:50.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In that case, focus solely on recovering.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.26,0:16:53.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And we'll need to give you \Na new name and status.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.31,0:16:56.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll make you the adopted \Nson of a ruined noble.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.27,0:17:01.09,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll find a place in Almeria where \Nyou can serve as a local governor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.09,0:17:02.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Stay there until things settle down.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.37,0:17:07.41,Default,Don,0,0,0,,Thank you so much... for everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.41,0:17:08.69,Default,Don,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.27,0:17:14.20,Default,Don,0,0,0,,I don't know if this will even \Nslightly repay my debt to you,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.67,0:17:16.83,Default,Don,0,0,0,,but there is one thing I must tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.11,0:17:18.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.87,0:17:23.94,Default,Don,0,0,0,,My former master, First Prince \NGilbert, gave the emperor a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.94,0:17:29.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.34,0:17:36.64,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah, what is this urgent matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.64,0:17:39.69,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What has you in such a panic?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.69,0:17:41.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I will say it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.71,0:17:45.49,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Please stop drinking the Wine of Poinix.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.49,0:17:47.50,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Poinix...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.50,0:17:50.35,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You mean the wine produced \Nin Gilbert's fief
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.35,0:17:53.63,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,that he began offering \Nto the palace this year?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.63,0:17:54.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.69,0:17:56.33,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.60,0:18:01.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It is a fine wine that can act as a \Ntonic with continued consumption,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.81,0:18:06.68,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but if taken with a certain food, \Nit becomes a terrible poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.68,0:18:10.96,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Oh? And what is that certain food?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.39,0:18:13.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The food known as Dragon's Claw.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.97,0:18:17.30,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,The one that the crown prince \Nand I eat once a year
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.30,0:18:20.78,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,in a ritual honoring our ancestors?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.78,0:18:25.08,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes. It has been nearly a \Nyear since you received the wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.59,0:18:28.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,By drinking it regularly \Nwith the crown prince,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.26,0:18:32.59,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,you've basically proven that \Nit contains no poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.36,0:18:38.42,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So when the time comes, no one will \Nsuspect the Dragon's Claw's role in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.71,0:18:42.14,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Even if anyone considers it, \Nit'll be seen as an accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.14,0:18:47.34,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Which gives the murderer a perfect alibi.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.34,0:18:48.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.11,0:18:51.04,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You're certain about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.04,0:18:54.84,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A death-row criminal was offered \Nboth items and told that he'd be freed
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.84,0:18:57.22,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,if he consumed both and survived.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.22,0:18:59.07,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The result was immediate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.07,0:19:04.06,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,So if Crown Prince Albert and I \Ncarry out the ritual as usual,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.06,0:19:07.54,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,you're saying that both of us will die?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.54,0:19:09.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Precisely.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.44,0:19:16.05,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Well done, Noah. Impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.05,0:19:18.92,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You've done well to expose this plot.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.46,0:19:23.01,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Cruz. Summon Henry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.83,0:19:28.32,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Send soldiers to the First Prince's\Nmansion and launch an investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.32,0:19:29.27,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,At once.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.27,0:19:32.04,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah, you may take your leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.04,0:19:33.97,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I will contact you about your reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.97,0:19:34.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, sire.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.32,0:19:44.66,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,That night, the force that marched \Non the First Prince's mansion...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.30,0:19:52.09,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,found proof through a butler's \Ntestimony that experiments
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.09,0:19:56.85,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,were being conducted to test poisons \Non illegally traded slaves.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.28,0:20:04.28,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Gilbert's plan to seize the empire after\Nkilling the emperor and crown prince
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.28,0:20:08.81,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,was stopped by Prince Noah's counsel \Nbefore it could be carried out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.70,0:20:17.90,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Why does something feel wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.22,0:20:22.24,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The emperor seemed to have eyes \Nand ears everywhere until now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.06,0:20:27.99,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That was shown to me over and over again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.71,0:20:34.20,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,So why didn't he know what \Nwas going on this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.67,0:20:37.67,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Unless...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.67,0:20:50.01,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You are truly clever indeed, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.01,0:20:55.73,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Y-You already knew, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.73,0:20:57.02,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.02,0:21:01.48,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,In fact, I have not been drinking \Nthe Wine of Poinix at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.03,0:21:06.59,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I have been emperor too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.59,0:21:11.23,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I'm sure there are those \Nwho can wait no longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.56,0:21:14.95,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,But you do not seem to be one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.48,0:21:16.63,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.08,0:21:18.44,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.87,0:21:21.27,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah Ararat,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.27,0:21:24.94,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I hereby appoint you vice \Nminister of military affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.94,0:21:27.39,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You will serve concurrently \Nas minister of law.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.71,0:21:34.19,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I also name you governor-general \Nof the first army,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.19,0:21:36.43,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,also known as the imperial guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.86,0:21:39.19,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes, sire.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.58,0:21:42.29,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,What is this? What does this mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.64,0:21:46.24,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I do not intend to go \Ndown without a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.66,0:21:50.80,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,If my own son kills me, I'll be \Na laughingstock for generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.24,0:21:54.37,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,But if that does happen...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.37,0:21:58.34,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I want you to seize the capital \Nwith the imperial guard
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.34,0:22:01.51,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,and choose a suitable replacement.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.33,0:22:07.87,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He wants me... to choose the right \Nperson to be the next emperor?!
